node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":346,"closed_issues":2304,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T09:34:58Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-12-04T11:07:51Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T12:06:09Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in:\n\n- Godot 4.5\n- Godot 4.5 .NET\n\n### System information\n\nLinux Mint 22.2 - Godot v4.5 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER Mobile / Max-Q (TU104M)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a Joint3D node or any of its parent nodes is hidden (by toggling visibility), the Joint3D gizmo remains visible in the viewport regardless. This behavior is demonstrated in the images below. While the example is simple, in complex assemblies this causes significant visual clutter and makes it difficult to select or manipulate the Joint3D node.\n\nThis issue was previously reported, and a working fix was submitted to the **joint_3d_gizmo_plugin.cpp** file, but the pull request was never merged. The following code change fully resolves the problem (verified in a custom build):\n\n```\nvoid Joint3DGizmoPlugin::incremental_update_gizmos() {\n\tif (!current_gizmos.is_empty()) {\n\t\tHashSet<EditorNode3DGizmo *>::Iterator E = current_gizmos.find(last_drawn);\n\t\tif (E) {\n\t\t\t++E;\n\t\t}\n\t\tif (!E) {\n\t\t\tE = current_gizmos.begin();\n\t\t}\n\t\tEditorNode3DGizmo *next_gizmo = *E;\n\t\tNode3D *node = next_gizmo->get_node_3d();\n\t\tif (node->is_visible_in_tree()) {\n\t\t    redraw(next_gizmo);\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tlast_drawn = next_gizmo;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1046\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9460942a-1180-4209-bab6-da2ff4284ae0\" />\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1046\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/26c22548-5080-4b0d-8e4a-041e266c1af7\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a HingeJoint3D node (or any 3D Joint) and set it's Node_A and Node_B to separate RigidBody3D nodes.\n2. Toggle the HingeJoint3D node's visibility or any of its parent node's visibility in the scene editor.\n3. The HingeJoint3D Gizmo is always drawn regardless of visibility.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThe aformentioned step to reproduce are trivial and should suffice.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113555/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113555/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}